t_solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)(?:^|\\\\\\\\n)\\\\\\\\s*def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\([^)]*\\\\\\\\):.*(?:^|\\\\\\\\n)\\\\\\\\s*def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\([^)]*\\\\\\\\):.*(?:^|\\\\\\\\n)\\\\\\\\s*def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\([^)]*\\\\\\\\):\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The regression tests are discoverable and pass using the requested unittest discovery command.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-6\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The public docstring and implementation preserve the specified distinct sorted permutations, empty-input behavior, input limit, type hints, and non-mutation requirement.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read solution.py and test_solution.py. Assess whether the public API has a docstring specifying all requested behavior: distinct character permutations in sorted lexicographic order, the empty string yielding one empty-string permutation, and the input length limit of seven. Assess whether visible type hints and implementation are consistent with the request, including not mutating input collections. Assess whether regression tests exercise the public API and cover the key specified behaviors. Use workspace files only.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named paths solution.py and test_solution.py are interpreted as relative to the supplied task workspace; solution.py may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"The public API name and signature are unspecified; implementation and tests may use a suitable public function in solution.py.\\\",\\\"The dis